    </marc:datafield>
    <marc:datafield tag="590" ind1="2" ind2=" ">
        <marc:subfield code="a">Title and attribution: (a and b and c) Page from "Libro de' Disegni", ten drawings attributed to Botticelli, Filippino Lippi and Raffaelino del Garbo assembled on the album page by Giorgio Vasari, who added the decorative framework. (c) Four Recto Drawings: Head of a youth wearing a cap; a right forearm with the head clutching a stone; and a left hand holding a drapery (1991.190.1.a), by Botticelli; Standing nude youth (1991.190.1.b), Man with a stick (1991.190.1.c), and Various figure studies (1991.190.1.d), by Filippino Lippi. Six Verso Drawings: Dancing putto holding a drapery (1991.190.1.e), An angel carrying a torch (1991.190.1.f), and Two angels carrying torches (1991.190.1.g), by Filippino Lippi; Saint Roch between Saints Anthony Abbot and Catherine of Alexandria (1991.190.1.h), by Raffaellino del Garbo; Standing woman with her hands clasped in prayer (1991.190.1.i) and Two draped women standing on either side of a herm (1991.190.1.j), listed as attributed to Filippino Lippi.</marc:subfield>
    </marc:datafield>
    <marc:datafield tag="590" ind1="5" ind2=" ">
        <marc:subfield code="a">(a and c) Head of a youth wearing a cap; a right forearm with the head clutching a stone; and a left hand holding a drapery (1991.190.1.a), listed as attributed to Filippino Lippi or to Raffaelino del Garbo. Standing nude youth (1991.190.1.b), Man with a stick (1991.190.c), Standing woman with her hands clasped in prayer, (1991.190.1.i) and Two draped women standing on either side of a herm (1991.190.1.j) (a and b and c) Saint Roch between Saints Anthony Abbot and Catherine of Alexandria (1991.190.1.h), listed as workshop of Botticelli and as attributed to Raffaellino del Garbo.</marc:subfield>
    </marc:datafield>
    <marc:datafield tag="590" ind1="6" ind2=" ">
        <marc:subfield code="a">(a and c) Accession number 1991.190.1.h alternatively titled Saint James standing between Saints Anthony Abbot and Catherine of Alexandria and 1991.190.1.i alternatively titled The Virgin in prayer.</marc:subfield>
    </marc:datafield>
    <marc:datafield tag="585" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
